"""Micras wall joint: the main board's side of the joint with a wall-sensor board (boards/wall).

A wall board stands upright on the main board, looking at the wall. Its 2x03 1.27 mm straight
header (components/hanxia/HX-PZ1.27-2x3P-ZZ) straddles the board's bottom edge: the board stands
between the header's two rows, its bottom edge on the 1.00 mm insulator, the short pins soldered
to pads on both its faces; the 3.90 mm pins go down into the 6 plated holes here, soldered under
the main board, and the insulator sits on the main board. No slot: the two rows of pins hold the
board. The wall board carries the sensor, the emitter resistor with its decoupling, and the
emitter's selector with its AC-coupled gate network; the main board keeps the shared emitter
current sink and each receiver's load at its ADC. Pad n here takes the header's pin n:

| Pad | Row, along the board | Pin | Main board net |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | front, left | OUT | the receiver's output: the ADC input and its load (Wall_Sensor_n) |
| 2 | back, left | GND | GND |
| 3 | front, middle | 3V3_A | 3V3_A (the receiver's collector) |
| 4 | back, middle | 3V3_D | 3V3_D (the emitter supply) |
| 5 | front, right | SINK | the shared constant-current sink's drain (EMITTER_SINK) |
| 6 | back, right | PWM | the selector's TIM3 channel (Wall_Sensor_PWM_n) |

Left and right as seen from the front of the wall board. The receiver's output sits at one corner;
its neighbours, beside it, across the board and diagonally, are 3V3_A, GND and 3V3_D, so neither
switching pin (PWM, SINK, at the other end) faces it or sits beside it.

Geometry (spec/wall.toml [header] and [joint], the joint's single source):
- Origin on the pattern's centre, under the wall board's mid-plane; the sensor looks along -y
  (rotation 0: the robot's forward). The front row (odd pads) at y = -0.635, the back row (even) at
  y = +0.635; along the row the pads sit at x = +1.27, 0, -1.27 for pins 1-2, 3-4, 5-6: the
  header's pin 1 is on the board's left seen from the front, the robot's right.
- Pads 1.10 mm round (pad 1 square) on 0.70 mm holes at 1.27 x 1.27 mm: the drawing recommends
  0.65 mm holes; 0.70 mm keeps room for JLCPCB's -0.08 mm finished-hole tolerance against the
  0.57 mm diagonal of the 0.40 mm pin. A 0.20 mm annular ring (JLCPCB's preferred for
  multilayer boards, rules/jlcpcb-pdk.toml) and 0.17 mm between pads.
- F.CrtYd: the header's 3.81 x 3.40 mm insulator, on which the wall board's 4.2 mm handle stands,
  plus 0.25 mm: 4.31 x 3.9 mm. The wall board is a paddle (spec/wall.toml [outline]): its neck
  widens from the 4.2 mm handle into the 8.4 mm blade, 3.06 mm or more over the main board outside
  this courtyard, and its overhang beside the handle, the blade's width by the board with its
  back-face parts (0.79 + 1.2 mm), is F.Fab here: main-board parts under it stay at or below
  2.55 mm (spec/wall.toml joint.under_blade; tests/test_main_layout.py). F.SilkS draws
  the insulator, the blade's front and pin 1.

The emitter, its resistor and its selector sit on the wall board (its W1, R1 and Q1):
`emitter_resistor` and `emitter_pulse_current` carry their values for the main board's emitter
checks (tests/test_wall.py and tests/test_wall_joint.py compare them with the wall board's).

Not a purchased part: copper on the main board, so it is excluded from the BOM and the placement
file (the header is the wall board's).
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Current", "Resistance")

PWM = io(Net)
SINK = io(Net)
V3V3_D = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)
OUT = io(Net)
V3V3_A = io(Power)

Component(
    name="JOINT",
    prefix="W",
    symbol=Symbol(library="WallJoint.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("WallJoint_2x03_P1.27mm.kicad_mod"),
    pins={
        "PWM": PWM,
        "SINK": SINK,
        "3V3_D": V3V3_D,
        "GND": GND,
        "OUT": OUT,
        "3V3_A": V3V3_A,
    },
    properties={
        # boards/wall/wall.zen R1: 3V3_D to the SFH 4550 anode on the wall board.
        "emitter_resistor": Resistance("3.3Ohm"),
        # The wall board's SFH 4550 (components/micras/WallSensor emitter_pulse_current): TA = 25 C,
        # D <= 0.2, tp <= 150 us (SFH 4550 v1.8 p.6, OHF05438).
        "emitter_pulse_current": Current("380mA"),
    },
    skip_bom=True,
)
